<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka T-bill yields fall in latest auction.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka T-bill yields fall in latest auction.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lankan treasury bill yields continued to decline, with weighted average of three, six and 12-month bills falling by 0.65 percentage points, 0.47 and 0.44 respectively, at Wednesday's auction, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>		  Bids received   Bids accepted     Avg yield</p>
<p>    3 months     6,011	     2,204	  16.49 (17.14)</p>
<p>    6 months     2,298		 650	  16.56 (17.03)</p>
<p>    12 months    6,542	     2,510	  16.67 (17.11)</p>
<p>    Total	 14,851	     5,364</p>
<p>NOTE - Bids in million rupees, yields in percent (previous week's yields in brackets). --Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
